    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Conjugation and structure of the future",
     "texto": [
      "«Werden» in the present: **ich werde, du wirst, er/sie/es wird, wir werden, ihr werdet, sie/Sie werden**.",
      "The auxiliary «werden» takes position 2 in the sentence, while the main verb with its lexical meaning goes in the infinitive at the end: **Nächste Woche werde ich nach Köln fahren**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Inversion with time expressions",
     "texto": [
      "If a time expression takes the first position, the auxiliary «werden» goes in second position and the subject comes straight after it: **Morgen werde ich viel lernen**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
